# Machine-written perf baselines.
#
# README.md here and .github/workflows/perf-regression.yaml both state that no
# `*.json` is committed and that a baseline is "never auto-committed": the first
# run on a chip writes `status="pending"` numbers that only become a baseline
# after a human reviews the uploaded artifact and flips them to `"confirmed"`.
# Without this file that first run leaves the working tree dirty, so a green
# nightly would still show up as uncommitted changes -- and `git add -A` would
# silently promote an unreviewed pending baseline into the repo.
#
# Promotion is therefore an explicit `git add -f <chip>/<suite>.json`, which is
# exactly the human act the flow asks for.
*.json
